    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy notice (POPIA)</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">Responsible party: Meridian Group.\n\nWhat we process: your name, employee number, contact details, department, attendance records, and — only at the moment an arrival or departure is detected or confirmed — your phone\'s location (with accuracy), the connected Wi-Fi network name (if enabled), battery level and basic device details (model, Android version, app version, installation ID).\n\nWhy: to record working time accurately and to prevent fraudulent attendance. Location is compared with your workplace boundary; your route is not tracked.\n\nWho sees it: you, and authorised managers and administrators of Meridian Group. Data is stored on Meridian\'s servers and is not sold or used for advertising.\n\nHow long: according to Meridian\'s retention policy; location details are pseudonymised after the configured location-retention period.\n\nYour rights: you may request access to or correction of your personal information (Profile → Request correction) and object to processing by contacting HR or Meridian\'s Information Officer. You may switch off location permissions at any time and use manual requests instead.</string>

